IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P6-art-51-52`

-- P6-annex-xi-xiii: Annexes XI, XII and XIII of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744
-- (the consolidated text of 27.7.2026 is a rendering with no legal effect). The Annexes were not changed by the Omnibus: one text.
-- Annex XI is "referred to in Article 53(1), point (a)" and Annex XII "in Article 53(1), point (b)": they say what the documentation and the information of a provider of a general-purpose AI model
-- must contain, so they follow Chapter V's group and Art 111(3) through the gate `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` (fork F-annex-group).
-- Annex XIII says what the Commission takes into account in a designation (Article 51(1)(b), Article 52(4)): it follows the group only.
-- Each function answers: NOTHING (not covered, NOTHING-kind) before the gate opens; otherwise JUST TRUE when the content is there and JUST FALSE when an item that is required is missing (FALSE-kind).
-- "Where applicable" is read as gating the whole item it stands in: an item that does not apply is not required (fork F-annex-where-applicable).
-- "At least" and "at a minimum" (the Annexes' opening words) make each list a floor: more information is no failure.

DECLARE `Annex XIII act` IS ONE OF
    `Annex XIII take into account the criteria for the designation of a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`

§ `Annex XI Section 1: information to be provided by all providers of general-purpose AI models`

-- Point 1: a general description of the model, "including" six items (a) to (f): the list is the floor the text sets ("shall contain at least the following information").
-- src:1913 | 1. A general description of the general-purpose AI model including:
-- src:1914 | (a) the tasks that the model is intended to perform and the type and nature of AI systems in which it can be integrated;
-- src:1915 | (b) the acceptable use policies applicable;
-- src:1916 | (c) the date of release and methods of distribution;
-- src:1917 | (d) the architecture and number of parameters;
-- src:1918 | (e) the modality (e.g. text, image) and format of inputs and outputs;
-- src:1919 | (f) the licence.
@ref Annex XI Section 1 point 1 (src:1913-1919)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description states the tasks that the model is intended to perform and the type and nature of AI systems in which it can be integrated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description states the acceptable use policies applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description states the date of release and methods of distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description states the architecture and number of parameters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description states the modality and format of inputs and outputs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description states the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XI Section 1 point 1 the general description of the model contains the information` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE JUST (    `the description states the tasks that the model is intended to perform and the type and nature of AI systems in which it can be integrated`
               AND `the description states the acceptable use policies applicable`
               AND `the description states the date of release and methods of distribution`
               AND `the description states the architecture and number of parameters`
               AND `the description states the modality and format of inputs and outputs`
               AND `the description states the licence`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall contain at least the following information ... 1. A general description of the general-purpose AI model including: (a) ... (f)" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

-- Point 2: a detailed description of the elements and of the process, "including" (a) to (e). Item (c) is "where applicable". Item (e) is "known or estimated energy consumption", and the sentence after the list
-- says that where it is unknown it "may be based on information about computational resources used": so (e) is met by stating the figure, or, when it is unknown, by basing it on the computational resources.
-- src:1920 | 2. A detailed description of the elements of the model referred to in point 1, and relevant information of the process for the development, including the following elements:
-- src:1921 | (a) the technical means (e.g. instructions of use, infrastructure, tools) required for the general-purpose AI model to be integrated in AI systems;
-- src:1922 | (b) the design specifications of the model and training process, including training methodologies and techniques, the key design choices including the rationale and assumptions made; what the model is designed to optimise for and the relevance of the different parameters, as applicable;
-- src:1923 | (c) information on the data used for training, testing and validation, where applicable, including the type and provenance of data and curation methodologies (e.g. cleaning, filtering, etc.), the number of data points, their scope and main characteristics; how the data was obtained and selected as well as all other measures to detect the unsuitability of data sources and methods to detect identifiable biases, where applicable;
-- src:1924 | (d) the computational resources used to train the model (e.g. number of floating point operations), training time, and other relevant details related to the training;
-- src:1925 | (e) known or estimated energy consumption of the model.
-- src:1926 | With regard to point (e), where the energy consumption of the model is unknown, the energy consumption may be based on information about computational resources used.
@ref Annex XI Section 1 point 2 (src:1920-1926)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description states the technical means required for the model to be integrated in AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description states the design specifications of the model and training process, including the key design choices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information on the data used for training, testing and validation is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description includes information on the data used for training, testing and validation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description states the computational resources used to train the model, the training time and other relevant details` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description states the known or estimated energy consumption of the model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the energy consumption of the model is unknown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description bases the energy consumption on information about computational resources used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XI Section 1 point 2 the detailed description of the elements and of the process contains the information` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE JUST (    `the description states the technical means required for the model to be integrated in AI systems`
               AND `the description states the design specifications of the model and training process, including the key design choices`
               AND ((NOT `information on the data used for training, testing and validation is applicable`) OR `the description includes information on the data used for training, testing and validation`)
               AND `the description states the computational resources used to train the model, the training time and other relevant details`
               AND (   `the description states the known or estimated energy consumption of the model`
                    OR (`the energy consumption of the model is unknown` AND `the description bases the energy consumption on information about computational resources used`)))
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall contain at least the following information ... 2. A detailed description of the elements of the model referred to in point 1, and relevant information of the process for the development, including the following elements: (a) ... (e)" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

-- "With regard to point (e), where the energy consumption of the model is unknown, the energy consumption may be based on information about computational resources used."
-- A "may" gated by "where": split site (ii); the answer is JUST FALSE when the energy consumption is known (the periods ruling's rule (b), "where" fails; fork F-XI-energy-where).
-- src:1926 | With regard to point (e), where the energy consumption of the model is unknown, the energy consumption may be based on information about computational resources used.
@ref Annex XI Section 1 point 2, sentence after point (e) (src:1926)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the energy consumption of the model is unknown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XI Section 1 point 2(e) the energy consumption may be based on information about computational resources used` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE IF `the energy consumption of the model is unknown`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the energy consumption of the model is unknown, the energy consumption may be based on information about computational resources used" ("where" fails: split site (ii), JUST FALSE)

-- The opening sentence: "The technical documentation referred to in Article 53(1), point (a) shall contain at least the following information as appropriate to the size and risk profile of the model".
-- The two points are taken as BOOLEAN inputs named for the answers of the functions above; "as appropriate to the size and risk profile of the model" is read as a further element:
-- information that is not appropriate to the size and risk profile of the model does not meet the sentence (fork F-XI-appropriate; the other reading: the phrase only lets the provider scale detail).
-- src:1912 | The technical documentation referred to in Article 53(1), point (a) shall contain at least the following information as appropriate to the size and risk profile of the model:
@ref Annex XI Section 1 opening sentence (src:1912)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the general description of the model contains the information of point 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the detailed description of the elements and of the process contains the information of point 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is appropriate to the size and risk profile of the model` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XI Section 1 the technical documentation contains at least the information as appropriate to the size and risk profile of the model` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE JUST (    `the general description of the model contains the information of point 1`
               AND `the detailed description of the elements and of the process contains the information of point 2`
               AND `the information is appropriate to the size and risk profile of the model`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall contain at least the following information as appropriate to the size and risk profile of the model" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

§ `Annex XI Section 2: additional information to be provided by providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk`

-- Point 1: the evaluation strategies. Points 2 and 3 are each "Where applicable".
-- src:1928 | Additional information to be provided by providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk
-- src:1929 | 1. A detailed description of the evaluation strategies, including evaluation results, on the basis of available public evaluation protocols and tools or otherwise of other evaluation methodologies. Evaluation strategies shall include evaluation criteria, metrics and the methodology on the identification of limitations.
-- src:1930 | 2. Where applicable, a detailed description of the measures put in place for the purpose of conducting internal and/or external adversarial testing (e.g. red teaming), model adaptations, including alignment and fine-tuning.
-- src:1931 | 3. Where applicable, a detailed description of the system architecture explaining how software components build or feed into each other and integrate into the overall processing.
@ref Annex XI Section 2 points 1 to 3 (src:1928-1931)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documentation describes the evaluation strategies, including evaluation results, criteria, metrics and the methodology on the identification of limitations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a description of the measures for adversarial testing is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documentation describes the measures put in place for internal or external adversarial testing and model adaptations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a description of the system architecture is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documentation describes the system architecture` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XI Section 2 the technical documentation contains the additional information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
        IF NOT `the model is a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Additional information to be provided by providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk"
        OTHERWISE JUST (    `the documentation describes the evaluation strategies, including evaluation results, criteria, metrics and the methodology on the identification of limitations`
                        AND ((NOT `a description of the measures for adversarial testing is applicable`) OR `the documentation describes the measures put in place for internal or external adversarial testing and model adaptations`)
                        AND ((NOT `a description of the system architecture is applicable`) OR `the documentation describes the system architecture`))
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Additional information to be provided ...: 1. A detailed description of the evaluation strategies ... 2. Where applicable ... 3. Where applicable ..." (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

§ `Annex XII: transparency information for downstream providers`

-- Point 1: a general description, "including" (a) to (h). Items (d) and (e) are "where applicable".
-- src:1935 | 1. A general description of the general-purpose AI model including:
-- src:1936 | (a) the tasks that the model is intended to perform and the type and nature of AI systems into which it can be integrated;
-- src:1937 | (b) the acceptable use policies applicable;
-- src:1938 | (c) the date of release and methods of distribution;
-- src:1939 | (d) how the model interacts, or can be used to interact, with hardware or software that is not part of the model itself, where applicable;
-- src:1940 | (e) the versions of relevant software related to the use of the general-purpose AI model, where applicable;
-- src:1941 | (f) the architecture and number of parameters;
-- src:1942 | (g) the modality (e.g. text, image) and format of inputs and outputs;
-- src:1943 | (h) the licence for the model.
@ref Annex XII point 1 (src:1935-1943)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the tasks that the model is intended to perform and the type and nature of AI systems into which it can be integrated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the acceptable use policies applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the date of release and methods of distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a description of how the model interacts with hardware or software that is not part of the model itself is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states how the model interacts, or can be used to interact, with hardware or software that is not part of the model itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the versions of relevant software related to the use of the model are applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the versions of relevant software related to the use of the model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the architecture and number of parameters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the modality and format of inputs and outputs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the licence for the model` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XII point 1 the general description of the model contains the information` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE JUST (    `the information states the tasks that the model is intended to perform and the type and nature of AI systems into which it can be integrated`
               AND `the information states the acceptable use policies applicable`
               AND `the information states the date of release and methods of distribution`
               AND ((NOT `a description of how the model interacts with hardware or software that is not part of the model itself is applicable`) OR `the information states how the model interacts, or can be used to interact, with hardware or software that is not part of the model itself`)
               AND ((NOT `the versions of relevant software related to the use of the model are applicable`) OR `the information states the versions of relevant software related to the use of the model`)
               AND `the information states the architecture and number of parameters`
               AND `the information states the modality and format of inputs and outputs`
               AND `the information states the licence for the model`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information referred to in Article 53(1), point (b) shall contain at least the following: 1. A general description ... including: (a) ... (h)" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

-- Point 2: a description of the elements and of the process, "including" (a) to (c). Item (c) is "where applicable".
-- src:1944 | 2. A description of the elements of the model and of the process for its development, including:
-- src:1945 | (a) the technical means (e.g. instructions for use, infrastructure, tools) required for the general-purpose AI model to be integrated into AI systems;
-- src:1946 | (b) the modality (e.g. text, image, etc.) and format of the inputs and outputs and their maximum size (e.g. context window length, etc.);
-- src:1947 | (c) information on the data used for training, testing and validation, where applicable, including the type and provenance of data and curation methodologies.
@ref Annex XII point 2 (src:1944-1947)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the technical means required for the model to be integrated into AI systems` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the modality and format of the inputs and outputs and their maximum size` IS A BOOLEAN
      `information on the data used for training, testing and validation is applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information includes information on the data used for training, testing and validation, including the type and provenance of data and curation methodologies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XII point 2 the description of the elements and of the process contains the information` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE JUST (    `the information states the technical means required for the model to be integrated into AI systems`
               AND `the information states the modality and format of the inputs and outputs and their maximum size`
               AND ((NOT `information on the data used for training, testing and validation is applicable`) OR `the information includes information on the data used for training, testing and validation, including the type and provenance of data and curation methodologies`))
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information referred to in Article 53(1), point (b) shall contain at least the following: ... 2. A description of the elements of the model and of the process for its development, including: (a) ... (c)" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

-- src:1934 | The information referred to in Article 53(1), point (b) shall contain at least the following:
@ref Annex XII opening sentence (src:1934)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the model` IS AN `AI model`
      `the model is a general-purpose AI model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the general description of the model contains the information of point 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the description of the elements and of the process contains the information of point 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XII the information contains at least the elements` MEANS
    IF `Art 51 the obligations of the provider of the model are owed on the date asked` `the date asked` `the model` `the model is a general-purpose AI model` EQUALS NOTHING
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives, to a general-purpose AI model, and Art 111(3) can give its provider until 2 August 2027
    ELSE JUST (`the general description of the model contains the information of point 1` AND `the description of the elements and of the process contains the information of point 2`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information referred to in Article 53(1), point (b) shall contain at least the following" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

§ `Annex XIII: criteria for the designation of a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`

-- "For the purpose of determining that a general-purpose AI model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in Article 51(1), point (a), the Commission shall take into account the following
-- criteria: (a) to (g)." A duty of the Commission, limited by its own wording to that purpose. All seven criteria are taken into account; an unmet one is JUST FALSE.
-- Criterion (c) is met by taking into account the compute "measured in floating point operations or indicated by a combination of other variables": either way is taking it into account.
-- src:1950 | For the purpose of determining that a general-purpose AI model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in Article 51(1), point (a), the Commission shall take into account the following criteria:
-- src:1951 | (a) the number of parameters of the model;
-- src:1952 | (b) the quality or size of the data set, for example measured through tokens;
-- src:1953 | (c) the amount of computation used for training the model, measured in floating point operations or indicated by a combination of other variables such as estimated cost of training, estimated time required for the training, or estimated energy consumption for the training;
-- src:1954 | (d) the input and output modalities of the model, such as text to text (large language models), text to image, multi-modality, and the state of the art thresholds for determining high-impact capabilities for each modality, and the specific type of inputs and outputs (e.g. biological sequences);
-- src:1955 | (e) the benchmarks and evaluations of capabilities of the model, including considering the number of tasks without additional training, adaptability to learn new, distinct tasks, its level of autonomy and scalability, the tools it has access to;
-- src:1956 | (f) whether it has a high impact on the internal market due to its reach, which shall be presumed when it has been made available to at least 10 000 registered business users established in the Union;
-- src:1957 | (g) the number of registered end-users.
@ref Annex XIII opening sentence and points (a) to (g) (src:1950-1957)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the purpose is to determine that a general-purpose AI model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in Article 51(1), point (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission takes into account the number of parameters of the model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission takes into account the quality or size of the data set` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission takes into account the amount of computation used for training the model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission takes into account the input and output modalities of the model and the state of the art thresholds for each modality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission takes into account the benchmarks and evaluations of capabilities of the model` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission takes into account whether the model has a high impact on the internal market due to its reach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission takes into account the number of registered end-users` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XIII the Commission has taken into account the criteria for the designation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT `the purpose is to determine that a general-purpose AI model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in Article 51(1), point (a)`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of determining that a general-purpose AI model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in Article 51(1), point (a)"
        OTHERWISE JUST (    `the Commission takes into account the number of parameters of the model`
                        AND `the Commission takes into account the quality or size of the data set`
                        AND `the Commission takes into account the amount of computation used for training the model`
                        AND `the Commission takes into account the input and output modalities of the model and the state of the art thresholds for each modality`
                        AND `the Commission takes into account the benchmarks and evaluations of capabilities of the model`
                        AND `the Commission takes into account whether the model has a high impact on the internal market due to its reach`
                        AND `the Commission takes into account the number of registered end-users`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Commission shall take into account the following criteria: (a) ... (g)" (a bare "shall" not done, taken case by case)

-- src:1950 | For the purpose of determining that a general-purpose AI model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in Article 51(1), point (a), the Commission shall take into account the following criteria:
@ref Annex XIII opening sentence (the duty; no time limit and no consequence in the text) (src:1950)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the purpose is to determine that a general-purpose AI model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in Article 51(1), point (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 51 official` `Annex XIII act`
`Annex XIII the Commission's duty to take the criteria into account` MEANS
    IF     (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
       AND `the purpose is to determine that a general-purpose AI model has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in Article 51(1), point (a)`
    THEN PARTY `Art 51 the Commission`
         MUST `Annex XIII take into account the criteria for the designation of a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk`
         -- no time limit and no consequence in the text (listed in NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path)
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed on these facts

-- Point (f): the impact on the internal market due to its reach "shall be presumed when it has been made available to at least 10 000 registered business users established in the Union".
-- A "when" condition on a presumption: when it fails, no presumption arises (JUST FALSE, "when" counts as "where"); a model with fewer users can still have such an impact, shown otherwise.
-- src:1956 | (f) whether it has a high impact on the internal market due to its reach, which shall be presumed when it has been made available to at least 10 000 registered business users established in the Union;
@ref Annex XIII point (f) (src:1956)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the number of registered business users established in the Union to which the model has been made available` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex XIII point (f) a high impact on the internal market due to its reach is presumed` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 51 the group applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter V applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the number of registered business users established in the Union to which the model has been made available` AT LEAST 10000
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which shall be presumed when it has been made available to at least 10 000 registered business users established in the Union" (a "when" condition: it fails, so no presumption)
